# LifePunch Website Organization

- Keep all website and portal work under the main `lifepunch/` folder.
- Use `lifepunch/website/` for a new public website or web app. Do not place website source at the repository root.
- Keep DXRP portal tab documentation, screenshots, exported schemas, and portal procedures in `lifepunch/portal/`.
- Do not mix website work into `lifepunch/addons/`, `lifepunch/gamemode/`, `lifepunch/server/`, or `lifepunch/admin-panel/`.
- If no website framework exists yet, propose the framework and folder layout before adding dependencies or generated project files.
- Suggested website layout: `lifepunch/website/src/`, `lifepunch/website/public/`, `lifepunch/website/content/`, and `lifepunch/website/docs/`.
- Keep reusable UI components in the website source tree, not in portal documentation folders.
- Treat `lifepunch/portal/config/*.json` as portal reference data. Do not duplicate it into website code unless a derived public-safe copy is needed.
- Never commit API keys, Discord webhook URLs, auth tokens, private player data, or production secrets. Use documented placeholders and keep sensitive values outside tracked files.
- Public website copy may reference LifePunch branding, servers, addons, and portal concepts, but operational procedures should remain in `lifepunch/portal/`.
- Add docs near the work: website build/run notes in `lifepunch/website/README.md`; portal process notes in the matching `lifepunch/portal/<area>/README.md`.
- Before changing live-facing server, addon, gamemode, rank, sanction, or economy information, confirm whether the change is documentation-only or requires owner approval.
